class_name CasinoPeople
extends RefCounted
## The people of the Casino's boss intro (the owner's reference sheet docs/art/reference/casino_patrons.webp and the
## Chairman's docs/art/reference/chairman.webp, October 17, 2026), each a HumanoidParts for the shared HumanoidRig,
## generated by code and kept simple like MarketplaceIntroVendor (the owner: simplified versions of the inspiration
## images, plain boxes and prisms): one material, one draw call a segment, a few panels for the long skirts and the coat.
## Built once each and cached (static, each with its own cache_key). CasinoPerson puts one on the rig and poses it.
##
## The looks: the "Wealthy Woman in Red" (LADY_IN_RED) and the two women who flank the Chairman (ESCORT_BLACK, ESCORT_BLONDE:
## the same build and gown, the owner: "the differences should just be in the colour of their dresses and their
## hairstyle"); the "Lady Luck" gambler (LADY_LUCK); the "Grimy Casino Patron" (GRIMY); the "Elite High-Roller"
## (HIGH_ROLLER); a croupier, bartender and waiter (DEALER, not in the reference); and the Chairman (CHAIRMAN: his look
## from chairman_face.gdshaderinc and HostileTakeoverModel.chairman()).
##
## Colour rules (GDD §2/§5): nothing here glows except the Chairman's tech lights, in the Corporate brand's blue (the
## reference's cyan is a hazard colour). Crimson, gold and burgundy are cloth and polished metal, never emissive; the
## lenses, the screens and the glass are dark or pale glass with a shine, never lit.
## Rig convention (HumanoidPiece): metres at design scale, +y up, -z forward (where the person faces), +x their right.
## DESIGN-TBD: the colours and proportions chosen, simplified from the sheets (listed in the task report for the owner).

enum Look { LADY_IN_RED, ESCORT_BLACK, ESCORT_BLONDE, LADY_LUCK, GRIMY, HIGH_ROLLER, DEALER, CHAIRMAN }

const CACHE_VERSION: String = "v1"

